{
  "name": "lane-commit",
  "mode": "tool",
  "description": "Main's lane lander lane-commit.sh and its Jet twin LaneCommit.jet (#5072 c15): queue a lane's patch, take the commit lock, drain every queued job (drop one whose caller died, skip a held lane or a frozen path, leave a job that touches a path already in the batch for the next round), apply each clean patch, run one precommit over the union of paths, commit each job with its own message, and on a failed batch precommit revert and land each job alone. The fixtures hold a repository whose gitdir is repo/ and whose worktree is repo/work (with one uncommitted file and a commit-msg hook that refuses REFUSE), a stand-in precommit (pre.sh) that fails on a bad path, the patches and messages, and run roots whose queues hold another lane's job (live caller pid 0, a dead one above pid_max), a hold switch, a live path freeze and an expired one. Commit dates are fixed, so each landed sha is the same on both sides: the batch and next-round cases land on top of lane B's commit, the fallback, dead-caller, hold and freeze cases land alone.",
